name zref
category Package
revision 80301
shortdesc A new reference scheme for LaTeX
longdesc This package offers a means to remove the limitation of only
longdesc five properties that is inherent in the way LaTeX's reference
longdesc system works. The package implements an extensible referencing
longdesc system, where properties may be defined and used in the course
longdesc of a document. It provides an interface for macro programmers
longdesc to access the new reference scheme and some modules that use
longdesc it. Modules available are: zref-user, use zref for traditional
longdesc labels and references; zref-abspage, retrieve absolute page
longdesc numbers (physical pages, as opposed to the logical page number
longdesc that is normally typeset when a page number is requested;
longdesc zref-lastpage, provide a zref-label for the last page of the
longdesc document; zref-nextpage, provide the page number of the next
longdesc page of the document; zref-totpages, provide the total number
longdesc of pages in the document; zref-pagelayout, provide the page
longdesc layout parameters of a each page (which may then be printed at
longdesc the end of the document); zref-perpage, make a counter reset
longdesc for each new page; zref-titleref, make section title or caption
longdesc text available through the reference system; zref-savepos, make
longdesc positions on a page available; zref-dotfill, controlled
longdesc dot-filling; zref-env, record the latest environment's name and
longdesc the line it started on; and zref-xr, provide the facilities of
longdesc the xr and xr-hyper packages.
